# PR merge policy (agents)

## Hard rule

**Do not merge a PR while required CI checks are failing or still pending**, unless the user explicitly overrides after you report the failure (e.g. emergency hotfix with known unrelated breakage).

Required checks include at minimum the **`pytest`** job on PRs to `beta` and `main`. Treat **`build-and-push`** / Docker validation the same way when present.

## Before merge

When the user asks to open, merge, or “push/merge” a PR:

1. Open the PR (feature branch → `beta`, or `beta` → `main` for releases).
2. Run `gh pr checks <number>` (or `gh pr view <number> --json statusCheckRollup`).
3. If checks are **pending**, wait with `gh pr checks <number> --watch --interval 15` (or poll until complete).
4. If checks **fail**, fix failures on the branch, push, and re-watch until green — **do not merge**.
5. Merge only when required checks **pass**, then report the merged PR URL and any post-merge notes (deploy `:beta`, etc.).

## When CI fails after merge

If a merge already landed with red CI:

1. Tell the user what failed and why (test name, log excerpt).
2. Cut a fix branch from `beta`, fix, PR, wait for green CI, then merge.

## Examples

```text
❌ User says "merge it" → gh pr merge immediately while pytest is failing
✅ User says "merge it" → gh pr checks --watch → fix test → push → green → gh pr merge

❌ "CI failed but I'll merge anyway" without telling the user
✅ "CI failed: test_batch_apply_tool_changes_mixed_success — fixing mock, will re-merge when green"
```

